Chapter: DiskTestRunner
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Codex chapter Opening (compile-frontend, parse-mode-flags)
  cites Codex chapter Diagnostic Bag (bag-errors)
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Build.md Phase B. The on-disk test runner: mount the boot volume, list what is
 on it, choose an entry by name, read the bytes back, and COMPILE them in this
 same program.

 The compiler arrives as a library. `Chapter: Opening` declares `codex-opening`
 and no `opening`, so it is citable, and `Codex` is a manifest quire: a cite of
 any of its chapters pulls the whole ordered unit `build/compiler-order.txt`
 names, minus that unit's own entry chapter. That is what lets one program
 compile another without a second boot.

 Every line prints a verdict of its own rather than one summary, because a
 bare-metal boot has no exit code to read: the serial log IS the result, and a
 stage that fails must say which stage.

Section: Reporting

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: The Compile

 `compile-frontend` is pure and Console-free, so a verdict costs no effects and
 needs no act block. Errors are counted rather than printed: a bare-metal serial
 log is the only channel and a failing chapter can produce hundreds.

 The bag is read ONCE per entry and both numbers come out of that one read: a
 second call would compile the chapter again to learn what it already knew.

  RunnerResult = record {
   rr-errors : Integer,
   rr-code : Integer
  }

  runner-run : Text -> RunnerResult
  runner-run (t) =
   let fe = compile-frontend t "Program" (parse-mode-flags "" 0)
   in let es = bag-errors (fe.bag)
   in RunnerResult { rr-errors = list-length es, rr-code = if list-length es == 0 then 0 else (list-at es 0).code }

 A read that failed and a chapter that would not compile are different answers
 and a summary must not merge them, so an unreadable entry is -1 rather than an
 error count of its own.

  runner-of : Maybe Text -> RunnerResult
  runner-of (src) =
   if is-none src then RunnerResult { rr-errors = 0 - 1, rr-code = 0 }
   else runner-run (from-maybe src "")

 The FIRST diagnostic code is what a `.failing` sidecar records, so printing it
 is what lets that half of the diff be made at all. The pairing itself stays on
 the host: the sidecars are not on the image, and putting them there is a
 namespace question rather than a runner one.

  runner-line : Text, RunnerResult -> Text
  runner-line (nm) (r) =
   if r.rr-errors < 0 then nm & " : READ FAILED"
   else if r.rr-errors == 0 then nm & " : errors=0 ok=yes"
   else nm & " : errors=" & show (r.rr-errors) & " ok=no first=CDX" & show (r.rr-code)

 EFI and SEED are the image's own directories, written by the image writer
 rather than put there by a caller. Everything else on the root is a subject.

  runner-skip : Text -> Boolean
  runner-skip (n) = if n == "EFI" then True else n == "SEED"

  runner-say : Text, RunnerResult -> [Console] Integer
  runner-say (nm) (r) = act
    print-line-uni (runner-line nm r)
    r.rr-errors
   end

  runner-walk : Fat16Volume, List Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console, Device.Block] Integer
  runner-walk (vol) (names) (i) (n) (bad) =
   if i >= n then bad
   else if runner-skip (list-at names i) then runner-walk vol names (i + 1) n bad
   else act
    src <- fat16-read-source vol (list-at names i)
    e <- runner-say (list-at names i) (runner-of src)
    runner-walk vol names (i + 1) n (if e == 0 then bad else bad + 1)
   end

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "=== DISK test runner ==="
    vol <- fat16-boot-volume
    print-line-uni ("volume    : bps=" & show (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector) & " ok=" & yn (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector == 512))
    if vol.vol-bytes-per-sector /= 512 then act
      print-line-uni "REFUSED   : no usable FAT16 volume; nothing to list"
      print-line-uni "=== runner done ==="
    end
    else act
    names <- fat16-list-root vol
    print-line-uni ("entries   : " & show (list-length names))
    print-line-uni "note      : each entry is compiled ALONE, with no cite resolution, so a chapter carrying cites reports every cited name undefined. Only a cite-free chapter's verdict is comparable with test.ps1's."
    bad <- runner-walk vol names 0 (list-length names) 0
    print-line-uni ("summary   : failed=" & show bad)
    print-line-uni "=== runner done ==="
    end
  end

